      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Exclusive: Watchdog asked to look into how James Watt got data of ex-crowdfunders he invited to join buy-back bid</p><p>James Watt, the BrewDog founder who <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/mar/02/brewdog-us-cannabis-drinks-500-jobs\">sold the debt-laden “punk” brewer earlier this year</a>, is the subject of complaints to the UK’s data privacy watchdog linked to his surprise bid to buy the company back, the Guardian has learned.</p><p>BrewDog’s brand, intellectual property, UK breweries and 11 bars were sold to the US cannabis and drinks firm Tilray in March for £33m, in a deal that rendered <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/feb/16/brewdog-sale-equity-punk-investors-steaming\">the shares of more than 200,000 crowdfunding investors worthless</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jul/17/brewdog-founder-james-watt-faces-data-privacy-complaints-over-emails-to-equity-punks\">Continue reading...</a>"
